 "output": "out",
 "coordinate_contract": "World-space normals, eye vector, refracted rays, exit point and light direction. Screen positions of 3D points are projected with the camera's own view-projection and used as offsets from the pixel's gl_FragCoord-based screen UV (TD texture convention, v up), so an unbent ray lands exactly on its own pixel. The offsets' x and y signs are measured per pixel by comparing the pixel's own projected position with its raster position (on the centre line of an odd-sized render, where both are 0, by the sign of the projected position's screen derivative unless the surface is nearly edge-on), so they follow the build's screen orientation; the flat-image reflection's camera-space offset also takes the projection matrix's own sign. Flip V flips the base UV and the vertical offsets together. Projected points are kept at least half as far from the camera as the surface. Only the 2D render mode and one camera per Render TOP are supported. Eye distance is straight-line for perspective and along the view axis for orthographic cameras, identical in both passes. Lengths (Thickness, Frost, Scene depth, Tint density and the ripple and film frequencies) are in scene units, scaled by Object size, the object's world radius over 1.45 (the family rule; this study's flattened demo torus fits to 0.872517, the default). Liquid noise and film swirl are looked up at the object-space position times the Geometry COMP's world scale (worldScale(), the cube root of |det(mat3(world))|), so the patterns stick to the object and count in world-sized steps; the noise drifts by uPhase, integrated on the CPU and wrapped at 256, and its slope is rescaled so Wobble does not depend on that scale. Equirectangular panorama in this study's convention (u = 0 toward +X, then +Z), not yet compared natively.",
 "color_contract": "Colour parameters are artistic values passed as data vectors. Colour parameters (Auto) follows project.workingColorSpace: pass-through keeps them as typed; a linear working space converts them from sRGB to linear in the shader (transfer curve only, no gamut conversion); presets were tuned in Pass Through. Output is premultiplied alpha; the material blends with One / One Minus Source Alpha, and its alpha follows the Refraction TOP's alpha ('covered'). Colour is capped at 1024 before output, alpha never. The back-face pass writes data (normal, minus the eye distance) to a 32-bit float target with blending and Dither off; it is never displayed. Under the ACEScg working colour space TouchDesigner forces TOPs to 16-bit float, which limits the stored distance to about 11 significant bits.",
 "schema_version": 1,
 "target_build": "Inspect host; written for TouchDesigner 2025.x (GLSL 4.60), not yet run natively",
 "external_dependencies": [],
 "native_status": "pending: not compiled or rendered in TouchDesigner yet; see validation.json",
